0000794105-26-000106	ExpenseExampleNarrativeTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			InstitutionalProspectus		en-US	0	32767	2	1	969	403		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000002563	These examples are intended to help you compare the cost of investing in the Fund with the cost of investing in other funds. The examples assume that you invest $10,000 in the Fund for the time periods indicated and then redeem all of your shares at the end of those periods. The examples also assume that your investment has a 5% return each year and that the Funds operating expenses remain the same.
0000794105-26-000106	PortfolioTurnoverHeading	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			InstitutionalProspectus		en-US	0	32767	2	1	101	18		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000002563	Portfolio Turnover
0000794105-26-000106	PortfolioTurnoverTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			InstitutionalProspectus		en-US	0	32767	2	1	691	511		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000002563	The Fund pays transaction costs, such as commissions, when it buys and sells securities (or turns over its portfolio). A higher portfolio turnover rate may indicate higher transaction costs and may result in higher taxes when Fund shares are held in a taxable account. These costs, which are not reflected in annual fund operating expenses or in the examples, affect the Funds performance. During the most recent fiscal year, the Funds portfolio turnover rate was 55 % of the average value of its portfolio.
0000794105-26-000106	StrategyHeading	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			InstitutionalProspectus		en-US	0	32767	2	1	130	31		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000002563	Principal Investment Strategies
0000794105-26-000106	StrategyNarrativeTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			InstitutionalProspectus		en-US	0	32767	2	1	1241	974		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000002563	The Fund employs an indexing investment approach designed to track the performance of the Bloomberg U.S. 1-5 Year Government/Credit Float Adjusted Index (the Target Index), which includes all medium and larger issues of U.S. government, investment-grade corporate, and investment-grade international dollar-denominated bonds that have maturities between 1 and 5 years and are publicly issued. Under normal circumstances, the Fund invests at least 80% of its net assets, plus the amount of any borrowings for investment purposes, in the bonds that make up the Target Index. The Fund invests by sampling the Target Index, meaning that it holds a range of securities that, in the aggregate, approximates the full Target Index in terms of key risk factors and other characteristics. The Fund maintains a dollar-weighted average maturity consistent with that of the Target Index. As of December 31, 2025, the dollar-weighted average maturity of the Target Index was 2.82 years.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002564			ETFProspectus	Risk=AuthorizedParticipantsRisk;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	1599	710		0	ETFProspectusMember_S000002564_AuthorizedParticipantsRiskMember	 Authorized Participants . Only Authorized Participants may engage in creation or redemption transactions directly with the Fund. The Fund has a limited number of financial institutions that may act as Authorized Participants. The Funds Authorized Participants are not obligated to engage in creation or redemption transactions. To the extent that the Funds Authorized Participants are unable to or choose not to proceed with creation and/or redemption transactions with respect to the Fund and no other Authorized Participants step forward to engage in creation or redemption transactions with the Fund, the Funds ETF Shares may trade at a discount to NAV and possibly face trading halts and/or delisting.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002564			InstitutionalSelectProspectus	Risk=InvestingInBondMarketsRisk;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	1456	1149		0	InstitutionalSelectProspectusMember_S000002564_InvestingInBondMarketsRiskMember	 Investing in Bond Markets . The Fund may be impacted by the general condition of the bond markets and by factors that affect bonds and bond issuers. For example, as a general rule, bond prices and interest rates move in opposite directions. When interest rates rise, bond prices tend to fall, and when interest rates fall, bond prices tend to go up. Bond income also is affected by changes in interest rates. Interest rates can rise or fall for a number of reasons, including, but not limited to, central bank monetary policy, inflationary or deflationary pressures, and changes in general market and economic conditions. Changing interest rates, including, but not limited to, rates that fall below zero, could have unpredictable effects on the overall market and may expose the bond markets in particular to heightened volatility and potential illiquidity. The degree to which the Fund is impacted by certain bond market risks may vary based on factors disclosed in its principal investment strategies, such as the types of bonds in which it invests and the overall credit quality, average maturity, and/or average duration of its bond holdings.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000019554			RetailProspectus	Risk=RiskLoseMoney;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	282	88		0	RetailProspectusMember_S000019554_RiskLoseMoneyMember	As with any investment, an investment in the Fund could lose money over any time period.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002564			ETFProspectus	Risk=ExtensionRisk;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	1076	312		0	ETFProspectusMember_S000002564_ExtensionRiskMember	 Extension Risk . During periods of rising interest rates, certain bonds held by the Fund may be paid off substantially more slowly than originally anticipated. As a result, the value of the bonds may fall, resulting in a decline in the Funds income and a potential loss in the value of the Funds investments.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			ETFProspectus	Risk=RiskLoseMoney;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	157	88		0	ETFProspectusMember_S000002563_RiskLoseMoneyMember	As with any investment, an investment in the Fund could lose money over any time period.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000025158			InstitutionalProspectus	Risk=BondLiquidityRisk;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	644	263		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000025158_BondLiquidityRiskMember	 Bond Liquidity Risk . If the Fund is unable to sell a security at an advantageous time or price, its returns may be reduced. There may be limited trading in the secondary market for certain debt securities, which could make them more difficult to value or sell.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002564			InstitutionalProspectus	Risk=InvestingInBondMarketsRisk;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	1456	1149		0	InstitutionalProspectusMember_S000002564_InvestingInBondMarketsRiskMember	 Investing in Bond Markets . The Fund may be impacted by the general condition of the bond markets and by factors that affect bonds and bond issuers. For example, as a general rule, bond prices and interest rates move in opposite directions. When interest rates rise, bond prices tend to fall, and when interest rates fall, bond prices tend to go up. Bond income also is affected by changes in interest rates. Interest rates can rise or fall for a number of reasons, including, but not limited to, central bank monetary policy, inflationary or deflationary pressures, and changes in general market and economic conditions. Changing interest rates, including, but not limited to, rates that fall below zero, could have unpredictable effects on the overall market and may expose the bond markets in particular to heightened volatility and potential illiquidity. The degree to which the Fund is impacted by certain bond market risks may vary based on factors disclosed in its principal investment strategies, such as the types of bonds in which it invests and the overall credit quality, average maturity, and/or average duration of its bond holdings.
0000794105-26-000106	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002563			AdmiralProspectus	Risk=CreditRisk;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	816	509		0	AdmiralProspectusMember_S000002563_CreditRiskMember	 Credit Risk . Credit risk refers to the chance that an issuer will default (fail to meet its credit obligations) or fail to make payments in a timely manner, which could result in a loss to the Fund. In addition, negative perceptions of an issuers ability to make payments can cause the price of a security to decline. While all debt securities are subject to credit risk to some extent, those with higher credit quality ratings generally pose less credit risk than those with lower credit quality ratings.
0000794105-26-000106	HighestQuarterlyReturnLabel	oef/2024q3	20251231	S000002564			ETFProspectus	Class=C000046844;	en-US	0	32767	3	1	106	7		0	ETFProspectusMember_S000002564_C000046844	Highest
