0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000031041				Risk=EarlyCloseLateCloseTradingHaltRisk;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	613	336		0	S000031041_EarlyCloseLateCloseTradingHaltRiskMember	? Early Close/Late Close/Trading Halt Risk  An exchange or market may close early, close late or issue trading halts on specific securities or financial instruments. In these circumstances, the Fund may be unable to rebalance its portfolio, may be unable to accurately price its investments and/or may incur substantial trading losses.
0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000050775				Risk=MarketPriceRisk;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	734	457		0	S000050775_MarketPriceRiskMember	? Market Price Variance Risk  Investors buy and sell Fund shares in the secondary market at market prices. Market prices may be different from the NAV per share of the Fund (i.e., the secondary market price may trade at a price greater than NAV (a premium) or less than NAV (a discount)). The market price of the Funds shares will fluctuate in response to changes in the value of the Funds holdings, supply and demand for shares and other market factors.
0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000054590				Risk=RiskLoseMoney;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	145	46		0	S000054590_RiskLoseMoneyMember	You could lose money by investing in the Fund.
0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000039732				Risk=ForeignEMMarketsRisk;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	1007	730		0	S000039732_ForeignEMMarketsRiskMember	? Foreign Investments Risk  Exposure to securities of foreign issuers may provide the Fund with increased risk. Foreign investments may be more susceptible to political, social, economic and regional factors than may be the case with U.S. securities. In addition, markets for foreign investments are usually less liquid, more volatile and significantly smaller than markets for U.S. securities, which may affect, among other things, the Funds ability to purchase or sell foreign investments at appropriate times and prices. Because of differences in settlement times and/or foreign market holidays, transactions in a foreign market may take place one or more days after the necessary exposure to these investments is determined.
0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000059653				Risk=MarketPriceRisk;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	734	457		0	S000059653_MarketPriceRiskMember	? Market Price Variance Risk  Investors buy and sell Fund shares in the secondary market at market prices. Market prices may be different from the NAV per share of the Fund (i.e., the secondary market price may trade at a price greater than NAV (a premium) or less than NAV (a discount)). The market price of the Funds shares will fluctuate in response to changes in the value of the Funds holdings, supply and demand for shares and other market factors.
0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000078011				Risk=AustraliaInvestmentRisk;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	962	511		0	S000078011_AustraliaInvestmentRiskMember	? Australia Investments Risk  Investments in securities of issuers in Australia countries involve risks that are specific to Australia, including certain legal, regulatory, political and economic risks. The Australian economy is heavily dependent on exports from the certain commodity markets, including energy and mining sectors, and is vulnerable to price changes in commodity markets. In addition, Australia is dependent on trade and economic conditions in other countries can impact the Australian economy.
0001174610-26-000065	RiskTextBlock	oef/2024q3	20250531	S000075630				Risk=IndustrialsRisk;	en-US	0	32767	2	1	548	272		0	S000075630_IndustrialsRiskMember	? Industrials Industry Risk  Companies in this industry may experience: adverse effects on stock prices by supply and demand both for their specific product or service and for industrials industry products in general; declining demand; and changing government regulation.
